<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: SOCCER-SLAVIA PRAGUE ADVANCE PAST MALMO IN UEFA CUP.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-SLAVIA PRAGUE ADVANCE PAST MALMO IN UEFA CUP.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Slavia Prague beat Malmo FF 3-1</p>
<p>on Tuesday to win their UEFA Cup first round second leg matchup</p>
<p>5-2 on aggregate.</p>
<p>Slavia had several early scoring chances finally</p>
<p>capitalising on midfielder Martin Penicka's header in the 13th</p>
<p>minute to put the last season's Czech league champions ahead</p>
<p>1-0.</p>
<p>Attacker Robert Vagner then made it 2-0 heading a cross</p>
<p>from the right corner by midfielder Robert Horvath past a</p>
<p>defenseless Jonnlie Fedel in the Malmo net.</p>
<p>Malmo went for broke from the opening minute of the second</p>
<p>half, constantly pressing last year's UEFA Cup semifinalists</p>
<p>with Jens Fjellstrom's header on a cross by Greger Andrievski</p>
<p>narrowing the gap to 2-1.</p>
<p>Slavia then put the game away in the 69th minute on Pavel</p>
<p>Horvath's penalty after Jiri Vavra was pulled down by Tommy</p>
<p>Jonsson in the box.</p>
<p>Teams:</p>
<p>Slavia - 1-Jan Stejskal, 2-Jiri Lerch (12-Jiri Vavra 46th),</p>
<p>4-Lubos Kubik (3-Lubos Kozel 87th), 5-Martin Hysky, 6-Pavel</p>
<p>Novotny, 8-Martin Penicka, 10-Daniel Smejkal (7-Edvard Lasota</p>
<p>63rd), 11-Robert Vagner, 16-Ivo Ulich, 19-Sladan Asanin,</p>
<p>23-Pavel Horvath</p>
<p>Malmo - 1-Jonnlie Fedel, 2-Jorgen Ohlsson, 3-Christian</p>
<p>Karlsson, 5-Tommy Jonsson, 7-Anders Andersson, 9-Jens</p>
<p>Fjellstrom, 10-Daniel Andersson, 11-Niclas Kindvell (22-Yskel</p>
<p>Osmanovski 73rd), 13-Matthias Thylander, 19-Hans Mattison,</p>
<p>24-Mikael Andersson (8-Greger Andrievski 46th minute)</p>
</text>
